From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cli: add check, offline admission of a configuration

A distribution that writes honk's configuration for it (a router's
configuration push, an init script that wraps the operator's file in an
entry of its own) needs to know before it starts or reloads honk whether
honk would take the configuration. honk-core has no such command: the
only way to find out is to start it, which binds listeners, attaches
programs and may take the instance lock from the running one. A reload
is no answer either, as SIGHUP keeps the old configuration on refusal
and reports only to the log.

Add `honk-core check`. It admits the -c entry offline as a start would:
the entry and its includes are parsed, validated and assembled, with the
configuration as its own active one, and routing and DNS are compiled
over the geodata it finds, the data directory's first. Nothing is bound,
attached, created or written. Every finding goes to standard error as
`<file>[:line[:column]]: <severity>[<code>]: <setting>: <message>`,
without values, which may be secrets; the command exits nonzero when a
start would refuse the configuration.

It shares the offline admission the native API validates candidates
with, which refuses a candidate whose geodata file is missing. A start
and a reload run without that file instead: its rules match nothing
until it is installed or fetched. A check that refused it would refuse
every first start, and every start where the data directory does not
outlive a reboot, before the geodata update ran. So the admission's
compile is split from that refusal (CapturedConfig::compile, which
validate now calls after it), geodata can load from a given data
directory (GeoSourceSet::load_from, which load calls with the
process-wide one), and offline::validate_for_start admits as a start
does, reporting a missing file as a geo-asset-missing warning.

The admission is the native API's, so the command needs the native-api
feature and a .dae entry, and is refused with --store db.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
